  "body": "- Impact\n- Final claim permanently reverts on campaigns funded with Fee-on-Transfer ERC20s; recipients cannot withdraw the remaining rewards.\n- Distributor’s balance ends up strictly less than the recorded campaign amount; funds remain stuck until governance intervenes, undermining distribution integrity.\n- Root Cause\n- In createCampaign the system computes campaignAmountMinusFees and then sets newCampaign.amount = campaignAmountMinusFees without validating what the distributor actually received. For FoT tokens, safeTransferFrom / safeTransfer delivers requested - fee_on_transfer , so distributor receives less than newCampaign.amount .\n- Distributor.claim computes toSend = amount - claimed[user][token].amount from the Merkle amounts and attempts to safeTransfer(toSend) from its balance. When cumulative claims equal the recorded campaign amount but the distributor holds less (due to FoT deductions), the final claim reverts for insufficient balance.\n- Attack Scenario\n- Creator approves and calls createCampaign with a FoT reward token and amount A.\n- DistributionCreator records newCampaign.amount = A - protocol_fee and transfers that nominal net to the distributor via safeTransferFrom .\n- Because the token is FoT, distributor actually receives (A - protocol_fee) - transfer_fee .\n- Claims proceed; early ones succeed. The last claim attempts to drain the remainder to reach newCampaign.amount and reverts because the distributor balance is lower than the recorded amount.\n- Recommended Mitigation Steps\n- Measure the distributor’s actual balance delta and record that value:\n  - before = IERC20(rewardToken).balanceOf(distributor)\n  - perform fee and distributor transfers\n  - after = IERC20(rewardToken).balanceOf(distributor)\n  - set newCampaign.amount = after - before\n- Apply the same delta-based approach for fee transfers, or explicitly document fee behavior when FoT tokens are used.\n- Alternatively:\n  - Denylist FoT tokens as reward tokens,\n  - Require pre-deposit and validate delta before recording,\n  - Document support only for non-FoT ERC20s.",
  "proof_of_concept": "// SPDX-License-Identifier: UNLICENSED\npragma solidity ^0.8.17;\n\nimport { Fixture } from \"../Fixture.t.sol\";\nimport { Distributor, MerkleTree } from \"../../contracts/Distributor.sol\";\nimport { IERC20 } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/IERC20.sol\";\nimport { CampaignParameters } from \"../../contracts/struct/CampaignParameters.sol\";\nimport { IAccessControlManager } from \"../../contracts/interfaces/IAccessControlManager.sol\";\n\ncontract C4PoC is Fixture {\n    uint256 internal constant maxDistribForOOG = 1e4;\n    uint256 internal constant nbrDistrib = 10;\n    uint32 internal initStartTime;\n    uint32 internal initEndTime;\n    uint32 internal startTime;\n    uint32 internal endTime;\n    uint32 internal numEpoch;\n\n    Distributor internal distributor;\n    FeeToken internal feeToken;\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n\n        initStartTime = uint32(block.timestamp);\n        numEpoch = 25;\n        initEndTime = startTime + numEpoch * EPOCH_DURATION;\n\n        vm.prank(governor);\n        creator.setFeeRecipient(dylan);\n\n        Distributor impl = new Distributor();\n        distributor = Distributor(deployUUPS(address(impl), hex\"\"));\n        distributor.initialize(IAccessControlManager(address(accessControlManager)));\n        vm.prank(governor);\n        creator.setNewDistributor(address(distributor));\n\n        feeToken = new FeeToken(\"FEE\", \"FEE\", 18, 10);\n        vm.startPrank(guardian);\n        address[] memory tokens = new address[](1);\n        uint256[] memory amounts = new uint256[](1);\n        tokens[0] = address(feeToken);\n        amounts[0] = 1e8;\n        creator.setRewardTokenMinAmounts(tokens, amounts);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        feeToken.mint(address(alice), 1e22);\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        feeToken.approve(address(creator), type(uint256).max);\n\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n\n    function test_submissionValidity() external {\n        bytes memory data = abi.encode(address(0));\n        uint256 amount = 100e18;\n        uint32 duration = EPOCH_DURATION;\n        CampaignParameters memory c = CampaignParameters({\n            campaignId: bytes32(0),\n            creator: address(0),\n            rewardToken: address(feeToken),\n            amount: amount,\n            campaignType: 1,\n            startTimestamp: uint32(block.timestamp),\n            duration: duration,\n            campaignData: data\n        });\n\n        vm.prank(alice);\n        bytes32 id = creator.createCampaign(c);\n\n        CampaignParameters memory created = creator.campaign(id);\n        uint256 recorded = created.amount;\n        uint256 bal = IERC20(address(feeToken)).balanceOf(address(distributor));\n        assertLt(bal, recorded);\n\n        address u1 = alice;\n        address u2 = bob;\n        uint256 a1 = (recorded * 60) / 100;\n        uint256 a2 = recorded;\n\n        bytes32 leaf1 = keccak256(abi.encode(u1, address(feeToken), a1));\n        bytes32 leaf2 = keccak256(abi.encode(u2, address(feeToken), a2));\n        bytes32 root;\n        if (leaf1 < leaf2) {\n            root = keccak256(abi.encode(leaf1, leaf2));\n        } else {\n            root = keccak256(abi.encode(leaf2, leaf1));\n        }\n\n        MerkleTree memory t = MerkleTree({ merkleRoot: root, ipfsHash: bytes32(0) });\n        vm.prank(governor);\n        distributor.updateTree(t);\n        vm.prank(governor);\n        distributor.setDisputePeriod(0);\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + EPOCH_DURATION + 1);\n\n        address[] memory users = new address[](1);\n        address[] memory tokens = new address[](1);\n        uint256[] memory amounts = new uint256[](1);\n        bytes32[][] memory proofs = new bytes32[][](1);\n        users[0] = u1;\n        tokens[0] = address(feeToken);\n        amounts[0] = a1;\n        proofs[0] = new bytes32[](1);\n        proofs[0][0] = leaf2;\n        vm.prank(u1);\n        distributor.claim(users, tokens, amounts, proofs);\n\n        address[] memory users2 = new address[](1);\n        address[] memory tokens2 = new address[](1);\n        uint256[] memory amounts2 = new uint256[](1);\n        bytes32[][] memory proofs2 = new bytes32[][](1);\n        users2[0] = u2;\n        tokens2[0] = address(feeToken);\n        amounts2[0] = a2;\n        proofs2[0] = new bytes32[](1);\n        proofs2[0][0] = leaf1;\n        vm.prank(u2);\n        vm.expectRevert();\n        distributor.claim(users2, tokens2, amounts2, proofs2);\n    }\n}\n\ncontract FeeToken {\n    string public name;\n    string public symbol;\n    uint8 public decimals;\n    uint256 public totalSupply;\n    mapping(address => uint256) public balanceOf;\n    mapping(address => mapping(address => uint256)) public allowance;\n    uint256 public feeBps;\n\n    constructor(string memory n, string memory s, uint8 d, uint256 fee) {\n        name = n;\n        symbol = s;\n        decimals = d;\n        feeBps = fee;\n    }\n\n    function mint(address to, uint256 amt) external {\n        totalSupply += amt;\n        balanceOf[to] += amt;\n    }\n\n    function approve(address spender, uint256 amt) external returns (bool) {\n        allowance[msg.sender][spender] = amt;\n        return true;\n    }\n\n    function transfer(address to, uint256 amt) external returns (bool) {\n        _transfer(msg.sender, to, amt);\n        return true;\n    }\n\n    function transferFrom(address from, address to, uint256 amt) external returns (bool) {\n        uint256 al = allowance[from][msg.sender];\n        require(al >= amt, \"allowance\");\n        unchecked { allowance[from][msg.sender] = al - amt; }\n        _transfer(from, to, amt);\n        return true;\n    }\n\n    function _transfer(address from, address to, uint256 amt) internal {\n        require(balanceOf[from] >= amt, \"balance\");\n        uint256 fee = (amt * feeBps) / 1000;\n        uint256 net = amt - fee;\n        unchecked {\n            balanceOf[from] -= amt;\n            balanceOf[to] += net;\n        }\n    }\n}",
